Changelog: 11-10-2026 00:44:36

Release front end: after Bump portal the commands come in the right order, numbered: 1. commit (no push yet), 2. test on a BC-250 (./install.sh, then bc250-bazzite-suite --source release, with what to check and what to do when something is wrong), 3. only then push and tag the portal. Step 2's hint lists the four steps (Pin, Bump portal, commit and test, push and tag), and docs/portal.md and the release_plan.py docstring say the same.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 00:31:51

Manual: Testing a portal release before its tag (docs/portal.md): install the portal from the checkout and start it with --source release, so the apps install from the pinned GitHub releases and are checked against their pins, as on a user's board; what to check, and what to do when something fails. Release step 5 links to it, and the release front end's portal commands show the test instead of "test the combination on a BC-250".

Changelog: 11-10-2026 00:18:14

Release front end as an app: tools/release.sh --install adds a launcher (~/.local/bin/bc250-release), an app menu entry and a Desktop icon for the checkout it is run from (--no-desktop-shortcut: menu entry only; --uninstall removes them). It is not part of the portal; the entry starts the checkout's own tool with its .venv-linux. The window shows its icon (tools/images/release-ui.png), and with the menu entry installed it keeps its desktop file name, so the task bar shows that icon. The manual serves tools/images as assets/tools/ and shows the small icon (release-ui-128.png) in the release section of docs/portal.md, with the install commands. New installer test tools/installer-tests/release-ui.sh, in CI and CLAUDE.md.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 00:11:07

Release front end: opening step 2 reads the tags again, so tags pushed from a terminal while the window is open show up without a restart (step 1 keeps what was typed in it). An empty pin list now says why: nothing tagged that is not pinned yet, with Fetch tags for tags made on another machine.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 00:04:34

CI: the pytest jobs check out the full history with its tags (fetch-depth: 0), as the versions job already did. tools/tests checks the shipped apps.toml, and once an app is bumped past its pinned release (step 1 of a release), that pin only passes when its tag exists; the default checkout has no tags, so the test failed in CI while it passed locally.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 21:37:45

Manual: Checking a release (docs/portal.md). A local build of a tag has the same content as the GitHub release, checked for bazzite-test-v0.1.0 and governor-v0.1.0: governor's tar is identical, bazzite-test's differs only in the build time in bc250_gui/_build_info.py. The .tar.gz checksum is not the same, because gzip output differs between zlib builds (Fedora's zlib-ng, Ubuntu's zlib). The build_release.py docstring and a release.yml comment, which said a local build gives the same files, now say this.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 21:23:00

Release tool tests no longer depend on the checksums pinned in portal/apps.toml. They failed once the first releases were pinned, because a local build (another mtime) never matches a real release. test_build_release pins bazzite-test to its own local build (build_release.py reads the manifest from one MANIFEST constant, so a test can point it at a copy) and gains a test that a wrong pin is refused; test_pin_app reads the old tag and checksum from the manifest; tools/installer-tests/release.sh runs on a copy of the checkout where pin_app.py pins bazzite-test and governor to their local builds, so the bundle and the fetched governor release are checked against a real pin. The release tools themselves behave as before.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 21:09:25

Release front end: no more "Failed to register with host portal" line in the terminal on Wayland. The tool has no .desktop file, so it no longer gives Qt a desktop file name to register.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:24:08

Release front end: tools/release.sh opens a window for the file edits of a release (tools/release_ui.py on tools/release_plan.py). Step 1 writes the new versions of the ticked apps (VERSION and every copy check_versions.py checks) and a "Release x.y.z." CHANGELOG entry with notes; step 2 pins the released apps in portal/apps.toml (tag and sha256 from the release's SHA256SUMS) and bumps the portal, at least as far as check_manifest.py asks, with a CHANGELOG entry listing the pins. It never commits, tags or pushes; it shows the git commands. check_manifest.py: the bump rule is now also a function of its own (required_bump), with the same results. tools/requirements-dev.txt adds PyQt6 for the window's tests. Manual (docs/portal.md), the development page and CLAUDE.md describe it.

Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:08:52

New app memory-manager (BC-250 Memory Manager): the VRAM split in CMOS, with the GTT, TTM limit and swap layout that go with it. CI runs its tests and its installer test (tools/installer-tests/memory-manager.sh) and shellchecks its installer at warning level; the portal lists it (changes_board); the manual has its chapter (docs/apps/memory-manager.md) and an internals page with the CMOS layout and the reads of two boards (docs/development/memory-manager.md); CLAUDE.md lists its checks.

